.\" Manual page for gpu-doctor. Preview with: man ./docs/gpu-doctor.1
.TH GPU-DOCTOR 1 "October 2026" "gpu-doctor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpu-doctor \- diagnose NVIDIA driver and CUDA problems on Ubuntu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpu-doctor
.RB [ \-\-json | \-\-report | \-\-list\-checks ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR ID [, ID ...]]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-color
.IR WHEN ]
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B gpu-doctor
.RB [ \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpu-doctor
inspects an Ubuntu system for the most common reasons an NVIDIA GPU or CUDA
does not work: no driver package, the kernel module not loaded, no module
built for the running kernel, missing kernel headers, the nouveau driver
holding the GPU, Secure Boot rejecting an unsigned module, a mismatch between
the loaded module and the userspace libraries, and a CUDA toolkit that is too
new for the driver.
.PP
Each check prints PASS, WARN, FAIL or SKIP, a one-line summary, an
explanation, and the exact commands that would fix the problem.
.PP
.B gpu-doctor is read-only.
It never changes the system and never runs the commands it suggests. It reads
files under
.IR /proc ,
.IR /sys ,
.I /var/lib/dpkg
and
.I /var/lib/dkms
directly and only runs a few read-only programs
.RB ( nvidia-smi ,
.BR mokutil ,
.BR modinfo ,
.BR nvcc ,
.BR prime-select ,
.BR lspci )
when they are available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON. The format is described in
.I /usr/share/doc/gpu-doctor/json-schema.json
and only changes incompatibly together with its
.B schema_version
field.
.TP
.B \-\-report
Print a block of text suitable for pasting into a forum post or bug report.
The hostname, username, home directory, UUIDs, serial numbers and MAC
addresses are redacted.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-checks
List the check identifiers and their titles, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check " " \fIID\fR
Run only the given check. May be repeated or given a comma-separated list.
Checks that the selected check depends on are run as well.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also show the evidence for every check: which file or command was looked at
and what it contained.
.TP
.BR \-\-color ", " \-\-colour " " \fIWHEN\fR
Colourise the output:
.BR auto " (the default),"
.BR always " or"
.BR never .
In
.B auto
mode colour is used only when standard output is a terminal and the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable is not set.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " DIR"
Inspect a copy of a system mounted at
.I DIR
instead of the running system. No commands are run in this mode.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH CHECKS
.TP
.B system_info
Operating system, kernel and architecture; warns if the system is not Ubuntu.
.TP
.B gpu_present
An NVIDIA display controller exists on the PCI bus.
.TP
.B driver_package
An Ubuntu NVIDIA driver package is installed; detects drivers installed with
NVIDIA's .run installer and leftovers from several driver branches.
.TP
.B kernel_module
The nvidia kernel module is loaded.
.TP
.B module_build
A module exists for the running kernel, either Canonical's prebuilt package or
a DKMS build.
.TP
.B kernel_headers
Headers for DKMS exist for the running kernel and will be installed for
future kernels.
.TP
.B nouveau
The open-source nouveau driver is not holding the GPU.
.TP
.B secure_boot
Secure Boot is not blocking an unsigned, locally built module.
.TP
.B version_mismatch
The loaded kernel module matches the installed userspace libraries.
.TP
.B nvidia_smi
nvidia-smi can talk to the driver.
.TP
.B cuda_compat
Every installed CUDA toolkit is supported by the installed driver.
.TP
.B container_toolkit
Docker can use the GPU (only when Docker is installed).
.TP
.B prime
On hybrid-graphics laptops, the NVIDIA GPU is not switched off.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every check passed or was skipped.
.TP
.B 1
At least one check produced a warning.
.TP
.B 2
At least one check failed.
.TP
.B 3
gpu-doctor itself failed: invalid arguments or an internal error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to a non-empty value, disables colour in
.B auto
mode. See https://no-color.org/.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Diagnose the system:
.B gpu-doctor
.TP
Only check Secure Boot and the kernel module:
.B gpu-doctor \-\-check secure_boot,kernel_module
.TP
Produce a redacted report for a forum post:
.B gpu-doctor \-\-report
.TP
Use from a script:
.B gpu-doctor \-\-json | jq \-r '.checks[] | select(.status == "fail") | .id'
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ubuntu-drivers (1),
.BR nvidia-smi (1),
.BR dkms (8),
.BR mokutil (1),
.BR modprobe.d (5)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/snehanagmoti/gpu-doctor/issues.
Please attach the output of
.BR "gpu-doctor \-\-report" .
